---
import DocsNav from "../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { evidenceHighlights, evidenceLevels, repositoryUrl } from "../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Evidence | Oxide Infer"
  description="Bounded correctness and performance records for Oxide Infer providers."
  active="Evidence"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Evidence</p>
    <h1>Each result keeps its boundary.</h1>
    <p>
      A result fixes the source, hardware, contract, baseline, method, and
      excluded claims.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Evidence" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Evidence levels</h2>
      <div class="evidence-level-grid">
        {evidenceLevels.map((item) => (
          <div class="evidence-level-card">
            <span>{item.level}</span>
            <div><h3>{item.name}</h3><p>{item.detail}</p></div>
            <small>{item.status}</small>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <h2>Current evidence status</h2>
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Result</th><th>Direction</th><th>Contract</th><th>Boundary</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {evidenceHighlights.map((item) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{item.value}</td>
              <td>{item.label}</td>
              <td>{item.detail}</td>
              <td>{item.sample}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Current-source H20 R1 qualification is complete.</strong>
        <p>
          The phase 2 record binds clean source <code>477b47a</code>, strict
          CUDA Clippy, seven release <code>sm_90a</code> lab tests, all nine
          permanent H20 runners, 89 passing case lines, and 12 named Graph
          cases.
        </p>
        <p>
          All 36 Compute Sanitizer cells pass without filters or suppressions.
          Performance, real-model engine execution, serving, and other GPUs
          remain outside this record.
        </p>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/h20-r1-phase2-qualification-477b47a-20260812.json`}>
          Current-source H20 phase 2 record
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Paged prefill has three explicit algorithms.</strong>
        <p>
          The caller selects direct, eight-warp, or sixteen-warp execution.
          The phase 2 record qualifies the current declared correctness,
          rejection, fixed-address Graph, and sanitizer paths.
        </p>
        <p>
          Historical performance records still predate the DeviceRegion and
          typed metadata-status paths. A matched current-source run is required
          before Oxide Infer can publish a current provider ranking.
        </p>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/h20-bf16-paged-prefill-token-parallel-correctness-20260807.json`}>
          Historical token-parallel correctness record
        </a>
        <span> · </span>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/h20-flashinfer-v0.6.16.post1-paged-prefill-long-eager-performance-20260807.json`}>
          Historical long-context performance record
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Engine interop is a simulated boundary.</strong>
        <p>
          The phase 2 H20 gate qualifies external pointers, the event-bridge
          path, zero adapter D2D copies, recovery, and all four sanitizer tools
          for direct single and HND paged decode. It does not run a model. A
          mistral.rs provider hit and model-output comparison remain open.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Fused append now uses a checked three-command path.</strong>
        <p>
          One validator builds a cache-bound append map. The mapped kernel then
          rotates Q and K and writes private K/V pages. A device-status copy
          reports semantic rejection at completion.
        </p>
        <p>
          The 2026-08-06 append records measured the earlier single-kernel path
          without exclusive-page ownership or typed status. Phase 2 qualifies
          the current path's declared correctness, valid-output and rejection
          Graph cases, and sanitizer matrix, but not current performance.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Current exclusions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No result proves model or serving speedup.</li>
        <li>Eager provider timing is not isolated kernel timing.</li>
        <li>Graph results cover fixed addresses and named paths only.</li>
        <li>Recorded graph node counts are declarations, not driver enumeration.</li>
        <li>H20 results do not qualify other GPU architectures.</li>
        <li>One shape does not establish a universal provider winner.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Read the complete <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/README.md`}>evidence index</a>
        {" "}for source hashes, fixtures, raw samples, and exclusions.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
